    feat(release): tag-triggered release workflow + pre-cut check + release docs
    
    RELEASE-TJ-008 gate 1 of 3 (gitreins task RELTOOL-1791152794779715762):
    give the repo a tag-triggered publish path so a future v1.3.0 cut can
    attach artifacts to the GitHub Release (v1.2.0 shipped with zero assets).
    
    - .github/workflows/release.yml: on push of v* tags (and
      workflow_dispatch with an explicit tag input, routed through env so a
      hand-typed input cannot inject shell). Resolves the tag, checks out
      the tag's tree, preflights the token (named ::error:: + exit 1 when
      GITHUB_TOKEN is empty or lacks push permission - no silent no-op),
      re-verifies pyproject version == tag, builds sdist+wheel with
      python -m build on Python 3.11, writes and verifies SHA256SUMS,
      creates the Release with gh release create --verify-tag, then re-views
      the Release and diffs its asset list against dist/ before reporting
      success. Never bumps pyproject and never creates tags.
    - scripts/release-cut-check.sh: read-only pre-cut validation - tag
      shape (vX.Y.Z), tag-not-already-exists, clean tree, pyproject version
      == tag, CI green on HEAD (gh run list; the TJ_RELEASE_CI_JSON env
      seam is documented for scratch verification; malformed CI data fails
      closed). Exits 2 on usage errors, 1 with named failures otherwise.
    - docs/releasing.md: the ordered runbook (version-prep commit -> CI
      green on that SHA -> release-cut-check -> tag -> workflow publishes
      -> verify assets on the Release object), noting that a v1.3.0 cut
      still requires explicit owner authorization (RELEASE-TJ-008).
    - tests/test_release_workflow.py: 15 cheap pins - the workflow YAML
      parses and carries the required structure; the check script's green
      path (scratch git clone --shared with the version bumped the way the
      real version-prep commit will) and its failure paths (existing tag,
      wrong version, red CI, malformed CI data) are all pinned.
    - .gitignore: dagger.db* (the harness dagger engine holds this
      rebuildable store open with this checkout as cwd; same class as the
      ignored board/Hilo caches) so a worker worktree reads clean.
    
    pyproject version untouched (1.2.0); no tags created. The publish path
    itself fires only on a real tag push.
    
